From fb8852ec47e634b19820bdaa4ea3afa0b260b6af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:48:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/41] moe cache: a sparse table without a RAM tier admits a
 routed expert it cannot register instead of declining

With a pin budget that refuses registrations, the remap hook of a sparse (mmap) table without a RAM tier declined
whenever a routed expert was neither resident nor registrable: a routing-dependent outcome, while the CUDA graph
capture gate assumes the take-over decision is constant per graph shape.  A graph captured on one outcome and
replayed on the other read the wrong source, so about 40 % of fresh loads at a 28 GB budget gave wrong output for the
whole load (identical with GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1: 6/6 correct).  Such an expert is now admitted regardless of the
admission rule, into a free slot or over the coldest resident the call does not route, filled from the mapping through
the capped per-table pinned bounce (shared with upload_pageable), and these tables also take the per-shape slot bound,
which guarantees that slot.  GGML_MOE_FORCE_ADMIT=0 restores the decline.

The per-shape bound also applies to a sparse table that runs without a tier for any other reason (the tier off or
dropped): a batch wider than its slots now declines where the cold read used to serve it.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu | 198 +++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 155 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu
index 06439cc5f..8bcdeb5a2 100644
